.TH "FWD SETUP" "1" "2026-08-16" "fwdit" "fwd setup Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-setup \- Create or update ~/.fwd/config.toml interactively or
entirely from flags.
.SH HOMEPAGE
\fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd setup
[OPTIONS] [BACKEND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create or update ~/.fwd/config.toml interactively or entirely from flags.
.PP
Setup automatically becomes non-interactive when stdout is not a TTY or
CLAUDECODE/CODEX_AGENT is set. Missing
required flags produce an exact invocation; pass --interactive to force
prompts. A positional backend such as
``fwd setup lambda`` is equivalent to ``fwd setup --backend lambda``.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fP <str>
Backend to configure: lambda, ssh, runpod, or slurm. Equivalent to
positional BACKEND.
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-name\fP <str>
Local fwd label for this connection; defaults to the backend name.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fP <str>
SSH hostname, IP, or Host alias from ~/.ssh/config.
.TP
\fB\-\-login\-host\fP <str>
Slurm cluster login hostname or SSH alias.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fP <str>
Remote username; optional for SSH aliases.
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fP <int>
SSH port.
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-path\fP <str>
SSH identity file; omit to use your SSH agent/config.
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-jump\fP <str>
External SSH host used to reach a non-public target, as user@host.
.TP
\fB\-\-extra\-ssh\-option\fP <str>
Additional raw SSH argv entry; repeat to preserve argument boundaries.
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\-base\fP <str>
Remote parent directory for project checkouts.
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fP <str>
Exact Lambda region code, or auto to choose from current capacity
(default: auto).
.TP
\fB\-\-preferred\-region\fP <str>
Preferred Lambda region code or prefix; repeat in priority order. Used
when --region is auto.
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\-type\fP <str>
Lambda Cloud instance type.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-key\-name\fP <str>
SSH public key name registered in Lambda Cloud.
.TP
\fB\-\-image\-id\fP <str>
Optional Lambda Cloud image id.
.TP
\fB\-\-fs\-mount\-path\fP <str>
Lambda persistent filesystem mount path.
.TP
\fB\-\-compute\-type\fP <str>
RunPod compute type: cpu (default) or gpu.
.TP
\fB\-\-cloud\-type\fP <str>
RunPod cloud pool: secure (default) or community.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\fP <str>
Default RunPod GPU id; used only with --compute-type gpu.
.TP
\fB\-\-image\fP <str>
Default RunPod container image.
.TP
\fB\-\-persistent\fP / \-\-no\-persistent
Use provider storage that survives compute termination (default: enabled).
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-center\-id\fP <str>
RunPod datacenter for the persistent network volume.
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\-gb\fP <int>
RunPod persistent volume size in GB.
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\-mount\-path\fP <str>
RunPod persistent volume mount path.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-proxy\fP / \-\-no\-allow\-proxy
Allow the RunPod SSH proxy fallback.
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\-prefix\fP <str>
Persistent remote directory for installed tools and caches.
.TP
\fB\-\-alloc\fP <str>
Slurm salloc flags.
.TP
\fB\-\-partition\fP <str>
Slurm partition.
.TP
\fB\-\-account\fP <str>
Slurm account.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-setup\fP <str>
Slurm shell line to run before allocation; repeat for multiple lines.
.TP
\fB\-\-make\-default\fP
Make this target the saved default. The first target is always made default.
.TP
\fB\-\-test\-connection\fP
Run read-only provider diagnostics after non-interactive setup.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fP
Overwrite an existing target with the same name without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fP
Force prompts even when stdout is redirected or an agent environment is
detected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
